       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Daily total:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. The usual maximum for an adult is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** Even with normal liver function, 6 g/day risks hepatotoxicity.\n\nHere are some options:\n1. **Standard dosing:** 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day), or 1000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day, the maximum).\n2. **Weight-based dosing:** For 70 kg, 15 mg/kg is about 1,000 mg per dose.\n3. **Intended dose:** If 2000 mg three times daily is what you meant, tell me and add a note on the rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first.\n\nWhich would you like me to enter?"
      }
