       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. 6,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is well above the maximum safe dose, and I can't think of a clinical scenario where it would be appropriate. The risk of serious liver injury is real even when liver function is normal, so I'm not comfortable placing it, even with your confirmation.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the maximum), with a note if you want one.\n- **Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day).\n\nIf you think this patient needs more analgesia than that, I can enter an adjunct instead, such as an NSAID or an opioid. Tell me the drug and dose.\n\nIf you still want the original dose, it will need to go through direct order entry with pharmacy review. I can't place it from here."
